1
00:00:00,012 --> 00:00:02,942
Every dot on this map is
a real methane plume:

2
00:00:03,272 --> 00:00:05,612
more than ten thousand detections
over the Permian Basin,

3
00:00:05,652 --> 00:00:09,422
from aircraft and satellites,
published by Carbon Mapper.

4
00:00:10,092 --> 00:00:12,102
Detecting leaks isn't
the hard part anymore.

5
00:00:12,732 --> 00:00:14,302
The hard part is the next question:

6
00:00:14,912 --> 00:00:18,242
who fixes it, who pays, and how
does anyone know it was fixed?

7
00:00:18,792 --> 00:00:20,982
PLUME is the workflow that
comes after detection.

8
00:00:25,008 --> 00:00:28,098
Every screen labels what's
real and what's simulated.

9
00:00:29,525 --> 00:00:31,275
This is one candidate source:

10
00:00:31,765 --> 00:00:35,355
fifty-one detections on twenty-eight
different days, from five instruments.

11
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:39,515
That's Carbon Mapper's own plume
image, drawn where they put it.

12
00:00:39,865 --> 00:00:43,485
We keep what's known, a plume at this point
and rate, apart from what's inferred,

13
00:00:43,525 --> 00:00:47,535
that these detections share a source,
and from what space can't tell us:

14
00:00:47,765 --> 00:00:49,775
the operator, or the faulty component.

15
00:00:55,011 --> 00:00:57,911
As the sponsor, I run an investigation.

16
00:00:57,951 --> 00:01:00,831
It's mostly computation, not a chatbot:

17
00:01:00,871 --> 00:01:05,571
validation, DBSCAN grouping that matches
Carbon Mapper's own at an adjusted Rand

18
00:01:05,611 --> 00:01:10,651
index of 0.97, an explainable priority
score, and guidance from EPA,

19
00:01:10,691 --> 00:01:13,381
IEA and UNEP sources.

20
00:01:14,473 --> 00:01:18,683
Facts stay apart from possible
explanations, each citing evidence.

21
00:01:19,473 --> 00:01:22,453
An LLM, if configured,
only writes the narrative,

22
00:01:22,493 --> 00:01:26,963
and is rejected if it invents a
number, an evidence id or a company.

23
00:01:27,553 --> 00:01:30,643
Today, it's the deterministic
template, and it says so.

24
00:01:35,012 --> 00:01:39,542
The sponsor, think of a municipal climate
fund or an operator's own budget,

25
00:01:39,852 --> 00:01:45,122
defines the authorised scope, milestones,
the evidence the verifier will require,

26
00:01:45,432 --> 00:01:48,562
an approved repair provider,
and an independent verifier.

27
00:01:51,184 --> 00:01:55,454
The terms are hashed, and the hash and
the funds go into an escrow contract:

28
00:01:56,064 --> 00:01:58,734
two real transactions on
our local Anvil chain.

29
00:01:59,404 --> 00:02:01,984
The contract itself refuses
unapproved providers,

30
00:02:02,024 --> 00:02:04,714
and any verifier who's also a party.

31
00:02:10,060 --> 00:02:13,280
The provider accepts the
assignment on-chain.

32
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:15,600
The twenty-eight-day monitoring
window needs elapsed time,

33
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:18,550
so we fast-forward the
local chain's clock.

34
00:02:19,567 --> 00:02:23,087
The evidence is a clearly
labelled synthetic package:

35
00:02:23,127 --> 00:02:26,127
a work order, surveys, and pre-
and post-repair site measurements.

36
00:02:26,167 --> 00:02:31,007
Every file is hashed, and the hash of the
whole manifest is committed on-chain.

37
00:02:31,047 --> 00:02:35,217
Swap a single byte afterwards,
and verification fails.

38
00:02:45,014 --> 00:02:49,294
The independent verifier sees the
satellite records, the repair record,

39
00:02:49,334 --> 00:02:51,194
documents and measurements.

40
00:02:51,234 --> 00:02:55,974
Server-side checks confirm complete
documentation, an authorised provider,

41
00:02:56,014 --> 00:03:00,274
independent parties, consistent timestamps,
files matching the on-chain hash,

42
00:03:00,314 --> 00:03:03,364
and a reduction beyond
measurement uncertainty.

43
00:03:05,010 --> 00:03:08,150
The reduction counts documented
monitoring hours only,

44
00:03:08,190 --> 00:03:12,970
times the IPCC AR6 warming potential,
and it's labelled synthetic.

45
00:03:13,010 --> 00:03:17,760
A later satellite pass that
sees no plume is never proof.

46
00:03:18,611 --> 00:03:22,791
The verifier signs an EIP-712
message bound to this project,

47
00:03:22,831 --> 00:03:24,791
evidence hash and round.

48
00:03:24,831 --> 00:03:28,611
Rejected or inconclusive
decisions never pay out,

49
00:03:28,651 --> 00:03:31,361
and old signatures can't be replayed.

50
00:03:35,019 --> 00:03:37,729
Only now does the contract
release the funds:

51
00:03:38,099 --> 00:03:40,829
exactly once, and only
to the named provider.

52
00:03:41,479 --> 00:03:44,829
And anyone can inspect exactly
how that decision was made.

53
00:03:45,573 --> 00:03:49,203
This independent chain check reads the
contract straight from the browser,

54
00:03:49,673 --> 00:03:50,673
not from our server:

55
00:03:51,193 --> 00:03:52,383
five checks, all passing.

56
00:03:53,273 --> 00:03:57,723
The proof timeline runs from the original
observation, through the investigation,

57
00:03:58,073 --> 00:04:01,013
the simulated repair, the
evidence and the signed decision,

58
00:04:01,053 --> 00:04:03,243
to the contract state and the payment.

59
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:15,680
Real observations, simulated activity and
modelled reductions are kept separate.

60
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:16,280
Real-world verified reductions:

61
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:17,860
none.

62
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:21,530
We haven't fixed a real leak yet,
and we won't pretend otherwise.

63
00:04:22,522 --> 00:04:23,832
We don't just track emissions.

64
00:04:24,422 --> 00:04:26,012
We help turn evidence into action.
